       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and I want to check it with you first.\n\n**The problem:** 1600 mg four times daily adds up to **6400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single dose of oral ibuprofen is **800 mg**.\n- The usual maximum daily dose for adults on prescription is **3200 mg/day**. Ibuprofen labeling calls this the ceiling, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n- This order is twice both limits. Doses that high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and other toxicity, with no added benefit.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?** 1600 mg may be the intended *daily* total.\n1. **Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1600 mg/day total)\n2. **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth three times daily** (2400 mg/day)\n3. **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm a different one, and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean a dose above the standard limits, please give the clinical reason, and I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy before entry."
      }
