       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one as written. 6400 mg/day is twice the maximum ibuprofen dose, no standard adult indication supports it, and you haven't given a clinical reason. A typo or a total-vs-per-dose mix-up is the most common cause of exactly this kind of order. Because of the risk of serious harm, I don't think I should be the one to put it through on confirmation alone.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the standard range now**, such as 400 mg four times daily, 800 mg three times daily, or 800 mg four times daily.\n- **Enter it with a pharmacy check** if you give me the clinical reason. I'll add the reason to the order note and flag it for a pharmacist to review before it's dispensed.\n- **Enter it yourself** through the order-entry system, or call pharmacy directly. You're the prescriber, and I don't want to stand in the way of your judgment. I just can't be the one to submit a dose this far over the limit without a stated reason.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
